tent using industry best practices to ensure every article is accurate, well-structured, and valuable for students, developers, and technology enthusiasts.\",\"sameAs\":[\"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/in\/mohit-kumar-99b556226\/\"],\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/author\/mohit-kumar\/\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530516510\",\"position\":1,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530516510\",\"name\":\"1. What is a framework\u00a0in\u00a0web development?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A framework is a pre-built set of tools, libraries, and best practices that helps developers build websites and applications faster. It saves you from writing repetitive code from scratch for every project.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530533916\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530533916\",\"name\":\"2. What is the difference between a framework and a library?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"A library is a tool you call when needed, while a framework controls the overall structure and\u00a0calls\u00a0your code. In short, you use a library, but a framework dictates how your application is built.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530548938\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530548938\",\"name\":\"3. Which is the best framework for web development in 2026?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"There's\u00a0no single \\\"best\\\" framework \u2014 it depends on your project. React and Next.js lead for frontend, while Django, Laravel, and Node.js remain top picks for backend development.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530573400\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530573400\",\"name\":\"4. Which framework is easiest to learn for beginners?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Vue.js and Django are considered the easiest to pick up due to their simple syntax and clear documentation.\u00a0They're\u00a0a great starting point if\u00a0you're\u00a0new to web development.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530584274\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530584274\",\"name\":\"5. What is the difference between frontend and backend frameworks?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Frontend frameworks handle what users see and interact with, like buttons and layouts. Backend frameworks manage servers, databases, and\u00a0the logic\u00a0running behind the scenes.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530599450\",\"position\":6,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/web-development-frameworks\/#faq-question-1784530599450\",\"name\":\"6. Is React a framework or a library?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"React is technically a JavaScript library, not a full framework. However, due to its ecosystem and component-based structure, mos